# .cursorrules — QuestAgent
# Cursor will load these rules into every AI interaction inside this project.

## Project identity
This is **QuestAgent**, a specialised AI agent for automated code analysis.
Primary language: Python 3.11+.
Entry point: `src/agent.py`
Test suite: `tests/`

## Architecture
- `src/agent.py`      — Multi-turn conversation loop using the Groq SDK
- `src/benchmark.py`  — Performance evaluation (0–10 000 scoring system)
- `ui/server.py`      — FastAPI bridge between the static UI and the agent
- `ui/static/`        — Browser frontend served by FastAPI
- `tests/`            — Pytest test suite
- `example/`          — Sample code files to review (bugs intentionally planted)

## Coding conventions
- Type-annotate every function signature.
- Use `dataclasses` or `pydantic` for structured data; avoid raw dicts where a type helps.
- Keep functions under 40 lines; extract helpers generously.
- Prefer f-strings over `.format()` or `%`.
- Never hard-code API keys or tokens. Always read from `os.environ`.
- Raise descriptive exceptions; never `except Exception: pass`.
- Write docstrings for every public function (Google style).

## Security rules (enforced by agent)
- All secrets → environment variables (`.env` + `python-dotenv`, never committed).
- SQL → parameterised queries only; no string interpolation.
- File paths → `pathlib.Path` with strict validation before `open()`.

## Testing
- Use `pytest` + `pytest-mock`.
- Every new feature needs a corresponding test.
- Run `pytest -q` before committing.
- Mock all Groq API calls in tests (never call the real API from tests).
  Patch `src.agent.client` and stub `client.chat.completions.create`.

## Groq SDK usage
- Use `groq.Groq()` (sync); the project does not currently use async.
- Model: `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` (defined in `MODEL` in `src/agent.py`).
- Always set `max_tokens`; never omit it.
- API key is read from `GROQ_API_KEY` via `python-dotenv`.

## Cursor-specific hints
- When generating new agent capabilities, follow the pattern in `src/agent.py`.
- When adding a new benchmark dimension, update `WEIGHTS` in `src/benchmark.py` so they sum to 1.0.
- Prefer modifying existing files over creating new ones unless the new responsibility is clearly distinct.
- Ask before adding new dependencies; update `requirements.txt` if approved.

## Commit message format
`<type>(<scope>): <short description>`
Types: feat, fix, perf, refactor, test, docs, chore
Example: `feat(agent): add streaming support for long reviews`
